From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_usb_power: optional BC1.2 detection

On the AXP813/AXP803 the driver enables BC1.2 detection at probe and on
each cable change. On the PinePhone, detection running while a host is
connected stops the USB gadget's network from sending (NCM TX stalls, no
error logged), and it sets the input current limit to 500 mA for a PC's
port; the PMIC keeps both across reboots.

With x-powers,no-bc-detection on the node, turn detection off at probe and
leave it off.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_usb_power.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_usb_power.c
@@ -1004,6 +1004,18 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (power->usb_bc_en_bit &&
+	    of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "x-powers,no-bc-detection")) {
+		/*
+		 * Off, and forgotten: the PMIC keeps the bit across reboots, and
+		 * the poll would enable it again on each cable change.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_field_write(power->usb_bc_en_bit, 0);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		power->usb_bc_en_bit = NULL;
+	}
+
 	if (power->usb_bc_en_bit) {
 		/* Enable USB Battery Charging specification detection */
 		ret = regmap_field_write(power->usb_bc_en_bit, 1);
